%U A399089 1,4,1,1,2,1,2,1,2,7,1,1,2,1,3,1,1,2,1,1,4
%N A399089 The maximum exponent in the prime factorization of the number preceding the n-th squarefree number.
%C A399089 Let d(k) = zeta(2) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 - 1/p^k). Then, the asymptotic density of the occurrences of 1 in this sequence is d(2) = 0.53071182... (A065469), and the asymptotic density of the occurrences of k >= 3 is d(k+1) - d(k).
%H A399089 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399089/b399089.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%F A399089 a(n) = A051903(A005117(n)-1).
%F A399089 a(A071403(n)) = A023504(n).
%F A399089 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = 1 + Sum_{k>=2} (1-d(k)) = 1.86972420871420434795..., where d(k) is defined in the Comments section.
%p A399089 subs(-infinity=0,map(t -> max(ifactors(t)[2][..,2]), select(NumberTheory:-IsSquareFree, [$2..200])-~ 1)); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 20 2026
%t A399089 emax[n_] := Max[FactorInteger[n][[;; , 2]]]; emax[1] = 0; emax /@ (Select[Range[2, 150], SquareFreeQ] - 1)
%o A399089 (PARI) list(kmax) = apply(x -> if(x == 2, 0, vecmax(factor(x-1)[,2])), select(issquarefree, [2..kmax]));
%o A399089 (Python)
%o A399089 # uses Python code from A005117
%o A399089 from sympy import factorint
%o A399089 def A399089(n): return max(factorint(A005117(n)-1).values()) if n>2 else 0 # _Chai Wah Wu_, Aug 20 2026
